{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592936-space-opera-gods-a-campaign-idea-please-kibitz","id":592936,"title":"Space Opera Gods (a campaign idea, please kibitz)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T11:13:50-07:00","id":592936,"title":"Space Opera Gods (a campaign idea, please kibitz)","content":"Try this idea, it's 12,000AD, and, on a terraformed planet half a galaxy away from ancient Earth,were civilization has come and gone and is fighting to come again, four patheons of gods compete to shape the future of their world. Each pantheon is connected to ancient pantheons, some of the members were gods on Earth in ancient times. Each pantheon promotes it own ideals. These pantheons are.<br /> <br /> <b>The Starry Host</b> Their virtues are Endurance, Expression, Intellect, and Valor. They uphold democracy, social justice, pan-sapient rights, and individual dignity, fairness, and freedom. Slogan: <b>Fairness and Freedom!</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Solar Court</b> Their virtues are Courage, Duty, Piety, and Order. They uphold glory and honor. They protect the weak, and the Weak owe their protectors service with honor. Slogan: <b>Glory!</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Lunar Covens</b> Their virtues are Courage, Harmony, Loyalty, and Vengeance. They uphold the tribesfolk in their many ways, and their freedom from corrupted and unnatural hierarchy. Slogan: <b>Praise to the Holy Mothers!</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Lodge of the Green</b> Their virtues are Conviction, Duty, Harmony, and Valor. They seek to free humanity of all false dichotomies by creating a new transhuman connection with nature. Slogan: <b>Become one with the Green!</b><br /> <br /> These guys are works in progress, but democracy, empire, tribalism, and utopianism, are the main themes of the pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-17-2015, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T13:33:11-07:00","id":594119,"title":"","content":"The planet that these groups are fighting for is called Albracca after a fortress in <i>Orlando Furioso. </i><br /> <br /> At the time of the campaign the planet is revering from a long period of economic and cultural collapse. Most people on Albracca live at an early modern level of technology and social organization. Think of the Earth in the late 17th and early 18th centuries. There are enclaves of higher technology. <b>The Starry Host</b> promotes a return to a higher technology. <b>The Lunar Covens</b> rejects the idea that technology should be brought back to the masses. Both <b>The Lodge of the Green</b> and <b>The Solar Court </b> feel elite control of technology is vital to the future of Abracca. Their reasons are very different.<br /> <br /> <b>The Starry Host</b> promotes mass literacy. All the other faction oppose mass literacy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-17-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T11:48:30-07:00","id":594888,"title":"","content":"<b>The Starry Host</b>'s PSP involves bringing individuals together as teams. It's a core belief with this pantheon that true individuality requires the support of the community to thrive, and that only fully self-realized individuals can create a true community.<br /> <br /> <b>The Solar Court</b>'s PSP involves hierarchy and legitimacy. It's largely about people realizing who their betters are and how to obey them. This pantheon has core beliefs resembling the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_chain_of_being\" target=\"_blank\">Great Chain of Being</a>.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lunar Covens</b> PSP is about Oaths and sworn duties. These folks can get the very elements of nature to contract with them. The core belief reflected here is that all reality is built of tribes and honor and trust brings them together.<br /> <br /> <b>The Lodge of the Green</b>'s PSP is about joining humanity to nature to new ways and transforming inherited traits. The Core belief is that humanity needs to become a new species or group of species to achieve transcendence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 07-18-2015, 02:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}